        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Pharaoh&#x27;s daughter, drawing the Hebrew infant out of the river and giving him a name, is for Ephrem the first prefiguration of the Gentile Church receiving the Word from among the Hebrews. The Egyptian princess does what her father refuses to do; the daughter of the oppressor saves the deliverer of the oppressed. Tewahedo cites this as a canonical anchor for Gentile-incorporation into the people of God.</p></aside>',
