        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>BUSH</strong> in which Jehovah appeared to Moses in the wilderness (Exodus 3:2; Acts 7:30). It is difficult to say what particular kind of plant or bush is here meant. Probably it was the mimosa or acacia. The words “in the bush” in Mark 12:26; Luke 20:37, mean “in the passage or paragraph on the bush;” i.e., in Exodus 3. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
