        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Loose thy shoe from off thy foot, for the place whereon thou standest is holy ground&#x27; — Ephrem hears in this not only Moses&#x27; singular calling but the rule for entering the sanctuary, that what carries the dust of the world is removed before standing where God has descended. Tewahedo carries this as the canonical warrant for entering the Beta Maryam barefoot, a practice preserved in every Tewahedo church to this day.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus III.2 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
