        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Water turned to blood at Moses&#x27; word is the sign of judgment; water turned to wine at Cana is the sign of joy. Ephrem reads the two miracles as a single canonical inclusio: the first prophet inverts the river to bring judgment on Egypt; the true Lord inverts the water-pots to bring gladness to the wedding. The Word who turned the Nile to blood for accusation turns the jars of purification into the wine of the new covenant.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus IV.5 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
