        "b",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>The hostile encounter at the lodging-place, where the Lord seems to seek Moses&#x27; life, Ephrem reads as a covenant-rupture answered by covenant-restoration: it is the failure to circumcise Moses&#x27; son that opens the breach, and Zipporah&#x27;s prompt circumcision that closes it. The Tewahedo reading harmonizes the canonical witness with Jub 48:1-2, which names Mastema as the immediate agent; the divine permission and the demonic accusation work together to vindicate the covenant.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus IV.20 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
