        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ELEAZAR G</strong> od has helped. (1.) The third son of Aaron (Exodus 6:23). His wife, a daughter of Putiel, bore him Phinehas (Exodus 6:25). After the death of Nadab and Abihu (Leviticus 10:12; Numbers 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Numbers 3:32). On Mount Hor he was clothed with the sacred vestments, which Moses took from off his brother Aaron and put upon him as successor to his father in the high priest’s office, which he held for more than twenty years (Numbers… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
