        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>NAHSHON</strong> sorcerer, the son of Aminadab, and prince of the children of Judah at the time of the first numbering of the tribes in the wilderness (Exodus 6:23). His sister Elisheba was the wife of Aaron. He died in the wilderness (Numbers 26:64, 65). His name occurs in the Greek form Naasson in the genealogy of Christ (Matt, 1:4; Luke 3:32). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
