        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>The lamb is to be set aside on the tenth day of the month — and on this very tenth day, Ephrem reads, the true Lamb entered Jerusalem to be set aside for the slaughter. The four days between the setting-aside and the killing correspond to the Holy-Week interval between Palm Sunday and Crucifixion. Tewahedo Pascal catechesis preserves this counting in its Holy-Week observances.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Hymns on the Crucifixion II.5-7 (NPNF S2 V13). PD.",
