        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MIXED MULTITUDE</strong> (Exodus 12:38), a class who accompanied the Israelites as they journeyed from Rameses to Succoth, the first stage of the Exodus. These were probably miscellaneous hangers-on to the Hebrews, whether Egyptians of the lower orders, or the remains of the Hyksos (see EGYPT; MOSES), as some think. The same thing happened on the return of the Jews from Babylon (Nehemiah 13:3), a “mixed multitude” accompanied them so far. <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
