        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (365).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on the Crucifixion</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>Moses stretches out the rod over the sea, and Ephrem hears in the gesture the shape of the Cross extended over the waters of baptism. The rod that splits the sea is the same wood that, in the new dispensation, splits the waters of death so that the baptized may walk through on dry ground. Tewahedo reads the Red Sea and the baptismal font as a single canonical passageway.</p></aside>',
