        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Israel passes through the sea on dry ground with the waters as a wall on either hand. Paul reads this as &#x27;baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea&#x27; (1 Cor 10:2); Ephrem follows Paul and reads Ex 14:22 as the founding scriptural figure of Christian baptism. Tewahedo carries this as the principal OT type of its baptismal liturgy: the people pass through the waters and emerge a people.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XIV.6 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
