        "Note",
        "<strong>The Song of the Sea.</strong> Often considered one of the oldest passages in the Hebrew Bible (along with Judges 5 and Numbers 23–24). Linguistic features — archaic suffixes, rare vocabulary, parallelism without later prose connectives — point to genuinely early Hebrew, perhaps 13th–12th century BCE. If so, the song may be older than the surrounding prose narrative that frames it.",
        "User original",
