        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;I will sing unto the Lord, for he hath triumphed gloriously&#x27; — the first canonical hymn of victory, sung on the shore of the sea by the redeemed. Ephrem treats Ex 15:1 as the prototype of all Pascal hymnody: every Easter song of the Church is a continuation of Moses&#x27; shore-song. Tewahedo mäzmur-tradition recognizes the Song of Moses among its earliest canonical warrants for hymnic praise after deliverance.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XV.1 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
