        "<strong>Miriam.</strong> Called <em>nevi’ah</em> (“prophetess”) here — only the second woman to receive that title in Hebrew scripture (after the unnamed mother of Isaiah’s sons in Isa 8:3 chronologically, but Miriam’s use is older textually). Her short song in 15:21 may be the original kernel from which the longer Song of the Sea grew, given its archaic form. Micah 6:4 lists her with Moses and Aaron as a joint leader of the exodus.",
