        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;I will rain bread from heaven for you&#x27; — the manna of the wilderness is for Ephrem the direct prophetic anchor of Jn 6: &#x27;I am the bread which came down from heaven.&#x27; The wilderness bread sustains the body for a day; the Eucharist sustains the soul for eternity. Tewahedo Anaphora cites Ex 16:4 and Jn 6 together as the OT-NT diptych of the eucharistic gift.</p></aside>',
