        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>QUAILS T</strong> he Israelites were twice relieved in their privation by a miraculous supply of quails, (1) in the wilderness of Sin (Exodus 16:13), and (2) again at Kibroth-hattaavah (q.v.), Numbers 11:31. God “rained flesh upon them as dust, and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea” (Psalm 78:27). The words in Numbers 11:31, according to the Authorized Version, appear to denote that the quails lay one above another to the thickness of two cubits above the ground. The Revised… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
