        "a",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>When Moses lifted up his hands Israel prevailed against Amalek; when he let them down Amalek prevailed. Ephrem reads the cruciform posture as the secret of the victory: Moses&#x27; arms outstretched are the Cross fore-figured, and the war is won not by the sword in the valley but by the cross-shape on the hill. Tewahedo carries this as the canonical OT type of Christian intercessory prayer in the cross-posture.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XVII.5 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
