        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>FIRST-BORN</strong> , SANCTIFICATION OF THE A peculiar sanctity was attached to the first-born both of man and of cattle. God claimed that the first-born males of man and of animals should be consecrated to him, the one as a priest (Exodus 19:22, 24), representing the family to which he belonged, and the other to be offered up in sacrifice (Genesis 4:4). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
