        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>CONCUBINE</strong> in the Bible denotes a female conjugally united to a man, but in a relation inferior to that of a wife. Among the early Jews, from various causes, the difference between a wife and a concubine was less marked than it would be amongst us. The concubine was a wife of secondary rank. There are various laws recorded providing for their protection (Exodus 21:7; Deuteronomy 21:10-14), and setting limits to the relation they sustained to the household to which they belonged… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
