        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>SPICES</strong> aromatic substances, of which several are named in Exodus 30. They were used in the sacred anointing oil (Exodus 25:6; 35:8; 1 Chronicles 9:29), and in embalming the dead (2 Chronicles 16:14; Luke 23:56; 24:1; John 19:39, 40). Spices were stored by Hezekiah in his treasure-house (2 Kings 20:13; Isaiah 39:2). <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
