        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MERCY-SEAT</strong> (Hebrews kapporeth, a “covering;” LXX. and N.T., hilasterion; Vulg., propitiatorium), the covering or lid of the ark of the covenant (q.v.). It was of acacia wood, overlaid with gold, or perhaps rather a plate of solid gold, 2 1/2 cubits long and 1 1/2 broad (Exodus 25:17; 30:6; 31:7). It is compared to the throne of grace (Hebrews 9:5; Ephesians 2:6). The holy of holies is called the “place of the mercy-seat” (1 Chronicles 28:11: Leviticus 16:2). It has been conjectured… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
