        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>The sign of Sabbath.</strong> The Sabbath as <em>‘ot</em> (sign) of the covenant — a weekly visible marker of Israelite identity (compare 31:13). For diaspora Jewish communities through history, Sabbath observance has been a central differentiating practice. The text’s anthropomorphism — God himself <em>nafash</em>, "was refreshed/took breath" — is striking; later philosophical Jewish tradition (Maimonides) reads it metaphorically, but the text’s plain sense is unembarrassed.',
