        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Moses breaks the first tablets at the foot of the mountain when he sees the calf; the second tablets are given after intercession and re-ascent. Ephrem reads the two givings as the canonical figure of the two Testaments: the first Adamic covenant broken at the foot of the mountain, the second covenant given through the One who ascends and descends. Tewahedo carries this as the principal OT figure of the OT-NT twofold canonical witness.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Exodus XXXII.10 (NPNF S2 V13, Gwynn/Schaff trans., Oxford 1898). PD.",
