        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>COMMANDMENTS</strong> , THE TEN (Exodus 34:28; Deuteronomy 10:4, marg. “ten words”) i.e., the Decalogue (q.v.), is a summary of the immutable moral law. These commandments were first given in their written form to the people of Israel when they were encamped at Sinai, about fifty days after they came out of Egypt (Exodus 19:10-25). They were written by the finger of God on two tables of stone. The first tables were broken by Moses when he brought them down from the mount (32:19), being thrown by… <em>[Reviewer: condense Easton's entry as needed.]</em>",
