        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Exodus</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>Moses descends with face shining and must put on a veil that the people may bear his presence. Paul reads the veil as the figure of the obscurity that remains over the OT until Christ takes it away (2 Cor 3:13-16). Ephrem follows Paul and reads Ex 34:30 as the canonical anchor of the veiled-to-unveiled progression: in the OT the prophet&#x27;s borrowed glory must be covered; in the NT the believer beholds the Lord&#x27;s own glory unveiled.</p></aside>',
