        "Note",
        '<strong>Pesaḥ (<em>פֶּסַח</em>).</strong> The verb <em>pasaḥ</em>, source of the festival name, occurs in v.13 ("I will pass over") and probably means "to limp," "to skip," or "to spare." The festival meal is to be eaten standing, dressed for travel — eternalizing the urgency of the Exodus night. The Christian Eucharist takes its institution from this meal (Mark 14:12–25). The Ethiopian Tewahedo Church preserves a strong Passover-Eucharist link in its liturgy.',
