        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The Song of the Sea.</strong> Exodus 15 is one of the oldest poetic strata of the Hebrew Bible (alongside Judges 5, the Song of Deborah). Its archaic Hebrew, parallelism, and triumphal celebration of God-as-warrior preserves a martial theology that later prophetic and wisdom traditions will both honor and complicate. The Ethiopian Tewahedo liturgy still incorporates this song. The image of God as warrior is uncomfortable for many modern readers; the Bible itself wrestles with it (cf. Isa 2:4, the swords-into-plowshares).",
